WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.470
Gaten Matarazzo seemingly came out of nowhere
to wow Netflix subscribers as Dustin Henderson

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:06.470
in Stranger Things.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.840
But there's more to Matarazzo than just D&amp;D
and Demogorgons.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.280
While Matarazzo is still quite young, there's
plenty you may not know about the young, curly-headed

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.280
celebrity.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.590
Before he was warming hearts as Dustin, Matarazzo
was belting out ballads on Broadway.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:24.000
At the tender age of eight, he played Benji
in the 2011 run of Priscilla, Queen of the

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.500
Desert, based on the 1994 film.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.810
From the glitz and glam of Priscilla, Matarazzo
went on to the role of Gavroche in the 2014

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.640
run of Les Misérables.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.090
Matarazzo is never far from his Broadway roots,
continuing to sing on various television shows

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.609
and regularly going to see stage performances.

00:00:39.609 --> 00:00:43.769
He's also set to play Jack in an upcoming
Hollywood Bowl production of Into the Woods,

00:00:43.769 --> 00:00:47.429
Stephen Sondheim's subversive take on classic
fairy tales.

00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:51.289
Many actors who start out on stage end up
leaving it behind for television and film,

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:55.379
but it seems that Matarazzo is content to
continue performing on stage and screen.

00:00:55.379 --> 00:00:59.200
"It's really cool to, like, have a job of
something that I love."

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:04.040
The young actor cites his older sister, Sabrina
Matarazzo, as part of his inspiration to pursue

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:05.420
a career in performance.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:09.460
Sabrina started out in community theater,
and has since had roles in a couple of short

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.890
films, as well as one episode of The Americans.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:15.060
But she's not the only talented Matarazzo
sibling.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.450
In 2015, Matarazzo congratulated his younger
brother, Carmen, on his first show, a community

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.670
theater production of Into the Woods Jr.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:25.310
It seems that all the Matarazzo kids have
a deep affinity for acting, and it's likely

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.320
we'll be seeing more of Sabrina and Carmen
in the future.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.200
In 2015, a year before Stranger Things made
him a household name, Matarazzo had a one-off

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.700
role on NBC's crime drama The Blacklist.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.670
The episode, titled "The Kenyon Family (No.
71)," features a polygamous cult leader harboring

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:42.060
some dangerous goods.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:46.680
Matarazzo plays a kid named Finn, who's been
brainwashed into carrying out a bombing attack.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.790
Once Stranger Things ends, Matarazzo will
have his pick of roles.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:53.610
It will be interesting to see if he sticks
with dramatic fare like The Blacklist or branches

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.130
out into different genres.

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:58.800
Even within the confines of Stranger Things,
he's shown an aptitude for comedy, drama,

00:01:58.800 --> 00:01:59.960
and horror.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:04.200
Born in Little Egg Harbor Township, New Jersey,
Matarazzo was only a couple hours away from

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.780
the bright lights of Broadway.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:10.729
Despite his rapid rise to fame and his ever-increasing
paycheck from Netflix, currently at $250,000

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:16.280
per episode for Stranger Things season three,
Matarazzo has not relocated to Hollywood.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.930
His life off the Stranger Things set seems
to be fairly typical of any American 16-year-old.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:25.680
He goes to school, and in 2019, he even went
to prom with his girlfriend, Lizzy Yu.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.379
It must be daunting, as a young person, to
have his entire life on display for millions

00:02:29.379 --> 00:02:33.650
of people to see, but Matarazzo seems to be
taking it in stride, living his life as normally

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.120
as he can, given the circumstances.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.560
The curly-headed actor is the lead singer
for a rock band called Work in Progress, a

00:02:40.569 --> 00:02:44.629
seven-person ensemble which includes both
of his siblings, along with a few friends.

00:02:44.629 --> 00:02:48.140
"Half the band is me and my brother and my
sister.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.239
That's three of us right there.

00:02:49.239 --> 00:02:52.319
And then the other three are, uh, they all
went to our school."

00:02:52.319 --> 00:02:56.879
The group has very diverse taste in music,
covering songs from bands including Led Zeppelin

00:02:56.879 --> 00:02:57.999
and The Black Keys.

00:02:57.999 --> 00:03:01.700
Speaking with The Aquarian, Matarazzo has
said that his two favorite bands to cover

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.459
are Pearl Jam and Green Day, as he's a big
fan of both Eddie Vedder and Billie Joe Armstrong.

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:10.319
According to Matarazzo, his dad introduced
him to Pearl Jam's music, and he's seen the

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:12.409
grunge band play multiple times.

00:03:12.409 --> 00:03:16.549
Work in Progress is recording its own original
songs now, with catchy titles like "Dream

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.440
Eater," which kind of sounds like something
that might come crawling out of the Upside

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.440
Down.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:25.480
As many dedicated fans know, Matarazzo was
born with a genetic condition called cleidocranial

00:03:25.499 --> 00:03:27.400
dysplasia, or CCD.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.150
This condition affects the development of
bones and teeth, and though Matarazzo seems

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.239
to have milder symptoms than many others with
the disorder, he was born without collar bones

00:03:35.239 --> 00:03:36.790
and is missing his front teeth.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.480
He's undergone several surgeries to mitigate
his symptoms...

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:45.240
"I've had two surgeries and I've had four
extractions, and um...I have more teeth than

00:03:45.249 --> 00:03:46.249
most people.

00:03:46.249 --> 00:03:48.299
I have extra teeth."

00:03:48.299 --> 00:03:52.560
...but his CCD does not seem to be preventing
him from living a full and exciting life,

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.180
though it did prevent him from getting acting
work early on.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:59.169
To this end, Matarazzo has chosen to raise
awareness of this rare disorder among his

00:03:59.169 --> 00:04:03.349
fan base, and he works to raise funds to help
those diagnosed who might not have access

00:04:03.349 --> 00:04:04.730
to the full breadth of treatment.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:09.950
He is working closely with the group CCD Smiles
as a spokesperson and collaborates on Dustin-themed

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.400
merchandise to raise funds for those in need.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:16.680
Matarazzo's Twitter and Instagram feeds are
a constant string of causes he hopes to bring

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.120
to his fans' attention.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.879
Most recently, he teamed up with Verizon to
help raise funds for first responders through

00:04:21.879 --> 00:04:23.710
the Gary Sinise Foundation.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:28.430
Matarazzo also supports a nonprofit restaurant
called Soul Kitchen, whose donated proceeds

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:31.840
go toward helping individuals struggling with
food insecurity.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.190
Perhaps having a genetic disorder has given
him a certain amount of perspective about

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:39.259
struggling with uncontrollable circumstances,
or perhaps it's just in his nature to pay

00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:40.640
his good fortune forward.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.590
Matarazzo appeared in a few music videos back
in 2017.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:48.620
The most well-known of these would probably
be Katy Perry's "Swish Swish" featuring Nicki

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:49.620
Minaj.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.349
In the video, Matarazzo plays Perry's teammate
on a basketball team with a reputation for

00:04:53.349 --> 00:04:54.879
being big-time losers.

00:04:54.879 --> 00:04:59.180
Matarazzo's nickname in the video is "Tragic
Johnson," and he's one among a lineup of lousy

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:00.180
ball players.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:04.560
In Computer Games' "Lost Boys Life" video,
Matarazzo plays the role of an adult who is,

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.880
to quote the lyrics, "living a lost boy's
life."

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:11.220
In the video, Matarazzo wakes up, goes to
his terrible job, argues with his boss, and

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.220
gets fired.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:15.750
But when everything seems bleak, he picks
up a guitar and starts leading a more personally

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.560
fulfilling life through music.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:22.080
Matarazzo made headlines when his Netflix
reality show, Prank Encounters, was announced.

00:05:22.099 --> 00:05:27.039
The show, which Matarazzo is both hosting
and producing, is set to air sometime in 2019.

00:05:27.039 --> 00:05:30.819
The premise of the show is that people show
up for their first day of work to find themselves

00:05:30.819 --> 00:05:32.460
besieged with weird pranks.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:35.960
Critics were concerned that vulnerable job
seekers were being fooled into taking fake

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.870
jobs and wasting precious time when they could
be seeking out real employment.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:44.199
Tricking the desperate doesn't seem like Matarazzo's
usual way of doing things, and both he and

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.560
Netflix worked to clear up the misunderstanding.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:50.570
"I just want to let everybody know that those
who participated were fully aware that it

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:54.120
was going to be a one-day gig going in...and
everybody was compensated."

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:58.551
Matarazzo is set to star as Rami, a young
camel crossing the desert in search of his

00:05:58.551 --> 00:06:01.199
human friend, in the 2020 film Hump.

00:06:01.199 --> 00:06:04.509
There's not a ton of information about this
movie as of right now, but he'll be working

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:08.840
alongside Simon Pegg, who's playing the villain,
and Ramy Youssef, who plays a human friend,

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:09.760
Omar.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:14.400
Rob Gibbs, an animator on Fern Gully: The
Last Rainforest, Toy Story 2, and Inside Out,

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:15.420
is directing.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:19.610
Once upon a time, Matarazzo's lisp prevented
him from getting any roles at all, and now

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:23.169
he'll be acting with only his voice as the
star of an animated film.

00:06:23.169 --> 00:06:25.380
